6. After M15 And M5 Taken Each Bars For Each Timeframes, Confirms Entry With At Least 2 Of 4 Confirmations Satisfied :
- 1. M15 Break of Structure (BOS). A Break of Structure is proof that a trend is healthy and moving forward. It requires the market to clear out old boundaries decisively.
      Sell Condition : Bearish BOS (Downtrend), Find the lowest point of the last downward wave (the previous Swing Low). A red candle must push below that floor and close its solid body underneath it.
      Buy Condition : Bullish BOS (Uptrend), Find the highest point of the last upward wave (the previous Swing High). A new green candle must push past that peak and close its solid body above that old high line.
      BOS Rule : If a candle only pokes its thin wick through the line but the solid body shrinks back and closes inside, it is a fake-out, not a BOS.
- 2. M5 Change of Character (CHoCH). CHoCH happens when a trend flips direction for the first time. It is the very first sign of a trend reversal.
      Sell Condition : Bullish CHoCH :
           - As Price falls into Fibonacci 0.618 - 0.786 zone, it was making a staircase downward (lower highs and lower lows).
           - Spot the final, lowest candle at the very bottom of the Fibonacci 0.618 - 0.786 zone.
           - Spot just slightly to the left candles and find the last minor "staircase peak" (the last minor high) that caused that final drop.
           - When a new green candle aggressively charges upward and closes its solid body above that last minor peak, the character of the market has changed from bearish to bullish.
      Buy Condition : Bullish CHoCH :
           - As Price falls into Fibonacci 0.618 - 0.786 zone, it was making a staircase downward (lower highs and lower lows).
           - Spot the final, lowest candle at the very bottom of the Fibonacci 0.618 - 0.786 zone.
           - Spot just slightly to the left candles and find the last minor "staircase peak" (the last minor high) that caused that final drop.
           - When a new green candle aggressively charges upward and closes its solid body above that last minor peak, the character of the market has changed from bearish to bullish.

- 3. M5 Equal Highs (EQH) & Equal Lows (EQL). These look like price has hit a flat, solid wall. In the Fibonacci 0.618 - 0.786 Zones.
      Sell Condition (EQH) : two or more candles whose top wicks peak out at the exact same price level, forming a straight horizontal ceiling. It looks like a double or triple top
      Buy Condition (EQL) : two or more candles whose bottom wicks drop down and step on the exact same price line, forming a flat floor.













